  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1111 AM CDT Thu Sep 3 2026\n\nA large and strong 500 hPa anticyclone will prevail across the\nsouthern half of United States for the next several days. This\nwill result in hot highs, warm lows, and primarily dry\nconditions continue through the rest of the week and into the\nweekend. The heat index may reach around 105F across the eastern\nzones for the next several afternoons. As a result, have issued\na heat advisory for the eastern zones through the end of the\nweekend. Neighbors wanted to keep the product as heat advisory\nand not change it to a heat warning, so this is why that\nproduct was issued as such. The NBM is showing some low pops\nacross the western zones Friday evening. Here, an isolated storm\ncannot be ruled out in close proximity to the sfc trof.\nOtherwise, the rest of the FA will see a dry forecast\ncontinuing. Highs will not change much over the next several\ndays. Hot highs, with values peaking from the upper 90s to low\n100s are expected. Warm lows are expected with values only\nbottoming out mainly in the 70s. The long range models and their\nensemble counterparts are not offering much hope for a weather\npattern change anytime soon. It looks like the strong ridge is\nexpected to prevail in several ensemble runs.",
